Restore the actor weight set after loading ref/teacher, whatever offload_train is.

Equivalent to upstream PR #2224 (https://github.com/THUDM/slime/pull/2224), open
since 2026-07-20 and not merged. PR #1903 fixes the same defect for the teacher
only; #2224 also covers the reference model, which is the more general form, so
that is the shape carried here. The `slime-opd-patch:` comment is the marker
the launcher greps for -- the guard alone is not usable as one, because
`if self._active_model_tag != "actor":` already appears in the training loop.

load_other_checkpoint() loads a checkpoint into the *live* model and leaves
_active_model_tag pointing at whatever it just loaded; it never switches back.
The only restore during init is guarded by `if self.args.offload_train`, which is
False unless --offload*, --colocate, or use_critic (advantage_estimator == "ppo")
is set.

With --opd-type megatron on a non-PPO estimator that guard is False, so after
init the live model holds the TEACHER's weights, and train_async.py's
update_weights() before the first rollout pushes the teacher to the SGLang
engines. Rollouts 0 and 1 are then generated by the teacher and trained on as if
they were the student's own on-policy samples -- silently, and with an inflated
reward. Measured: 399/512 correct at 6020 tokens/response versus a GRPO arm's
312/512 at 2282 on the same 64 prompts from the same SFT checkpoint.

The same path leaves the *reference* model live for any run with --use-kl-loss
and no offload, which after a resume serves the frozen reference instead of the
trained actor -- the case #2224 reports.

Setting --offload-train is not a workaround: on a non-critic run it makes
update_weights() take the `elif self.args.offload_train:` branch, which destroys
and rebuilds the NCCL WORLD group on every weight update and aborts under
ProcessGroupNCCL's watchdog.

diff --git a/slime/backends/megatron_utils/actor.py b/slime/backends/megatron_utils/actor.py
index 9bd65336..f584f9d5 100644
--- a/slime/backends/megatron_utils/actor.py
+++ b/slime/backends/megatron_utils/actor.py
@@ -178,9 +178,13 @@ class MegatronTrainRayActor(TrainRayActor):
         # empty cache after initialization
         clear_memory()
 
-        if self.args.offload_train:
-            # recover to actor in the end.
+        # slime-opd-patch: recover to actor in the end, whatever offload_train is.
+        # load_other_checkpoint leaves the last-loaded tag ("ref"/"teacher") live,
+        # and the rollout engines are seeded from whatever is live. Upstream #2224.
+        if self._active_model_tag != "actor":
             self._switch_model("actor")
+
+        if self.args.offload_train:
             self.sleep()
 
         self.rollout_engines = None
